WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:05.540
The air hummed, a space a few feet off the
ground rippling like a calm lake disturbed

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:07.819
by a stone thrown at its surface.

00:00:07.819 --> 00:00:10.700
Not that there was anyone around to see it.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:15.530
Which, of course, begged the age-old question
that has baffled philosophers, scientists,

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:19.600
and pretty much everyone with a working brain
for centuries.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.980
That being, if an interdimensional fracture
leading to an infinite multiverse of endlessly

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:28.240
recurring realities opens up in a hotel resort
bedroom in Mexico, and nobody is there to

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.900
see it, then did it really happen at all?

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.540
Well, in this instance, it really did.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:38.600
With a flash of light, a figure came tumbling
through the wormhole, fizzling out of existence

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.420
in one place only to arrive somewhere similar.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:47.600
Behind him, the purplish tear in the very
fabric of reality sealed itself shut as quickly

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.199
and inexplicably as it had opened.

00:00:50.199 --> 00:00:54.899
Sitting up, his Hawaiian shirt a disheveled
mess, the man blinked through his blurred

00:00:54.899 --> 00:00:55.899
vision.

00:00:55.899 --> 00:01:00.870
Eddie Brock was unsure if his headache was
the result of an intense hangover or the process

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:04.119
of being flung between universes, seemingly
at random.

00:01:04.119 --> 00:01:05.180
“Are we back?”

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:07.860
a voice in the back of Eddie’s head growled.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:13.659
“I have no idea, pal,” Eddie replied aloud,
looking around the vacant hotel room, the

00:01:13.659 --> 00:01:16.180
last of the daylight fading as the sun set.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:19.360
“We should eat,” the gravelly voice replied.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:20.520
“I’m hungry.”

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:23.729
“That’s all you ever think about,” he
replied.

00:01:23.729 --> 00:01:26.189
“I don’t even have any money on me.

00:01:26.189 --> 00:01:29.920
Besides, don’t you think we should try and
figure out where we are first?”

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:30.920
“Nope!”

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:36.050
In seconds, a dark, gooey substance morphed
over Eddie from head to toe, encasing him

00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:37.430
and his clothes.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:43.750
It formed a body, a towering, hulking monster
with wide, white eyes in the shape of teardrops.

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:47.250
Its mouth was filled with rows of long, razor-sharp
teeth.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:50.079
The black goo was constantly shifting.

00:01:50.079 --> 00:01:56.670
In fact, it was alive; an alien symbiote bonded
with its human host in order to survive.

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:59.560
Together, the symbiote and Eddie were Venom.

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:04.750
Bursting out of the hotel’s balcony as night
rapidly fell, Venom fired organic webs from

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:08.479
his wrists and swung through the city in search
of food.

00:02:08.479 --> 00:02:10.069
Agent Hardy hated fieldwork.

00:02:10.069 --> 00:02:15.120
He’d imagined working for the SCP Foundation
would be full of action and thrilling espionage

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:20.940
and had enrolled in undercover training, hoping
he’d be sent on missions to stealthily infiltrate

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:26.700
other anomalous organizations like the Church
of the Broken God or Global Occult Coalition.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:32.330
Instead, he was assigned to deep cover, which
was a Foundation euphemism for ‘stay put

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:35.400
and keep your eyes peeled just in case you
spot something unusual’.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:40.810
He had been stationed in Mexico City, and
was forced to work a menial job in a tiny

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:46.250
little convenience store to maintain cover;
a waste of his advanced combat and reconnaissance

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:48.010
training, he thought.

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:52.780
Agent Hardy badly wanted more, and found it
personally insulting that the Foundation saw

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:57.720
it fit to waste an asset like him, while he
should have been made part of one of their

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:59.790
Mobile Task Forces.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:04.330
Only adding to that perceived insult, was
the fact that nothing all that unusual or

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:08.260
even remotely anomalous ever seemed to happen
nearby.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:13.690
That is, until a seven-foot-tall, five-hundred-pound
oily black monster came barrelling into the

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:18.730
convenience store, barged its way over to
the confectionary aisle, and started shoveling

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:21.530
fistfuls of chocolate into its mouth.

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:26.190
All before dashing back out and swinging away
with as many candy bars as it could carry

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:27.190
in one arm.

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:31.220
“Hardy, if somebody robbed your store, that’s
a job for the local police department,”

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:36.560
the bored-voiced Foundation operator replied
over the radio as Agent Hardy contacted command.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:39.890
“No, not just somebody, something!”

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:42.890
Hardy yelled while the store’s customers
ran screaming from the scene.

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:44.299
“It’s a goddamn alien.

00:03:44.299 --> 00:03:46.150
I saw it with my own eyes.

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:47.150
It’s huge!”

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:51.250
“Hold on, one moment,” the operator replied,
before turning to a colleague, still audible

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:55.110
over the radio; meanwhile, Agent Hardy tapped
his foot impatiently.

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:57.380
“Didn’t we get a blip near there…

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:58.380
When?

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:01.230
I don’t know the exact time, about an hour
ago tops.

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:03.400
Any read on what it was?

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:04.900
Interdimensional disturbance?

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:05.900
Could be connected.”

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:07.799
“Look, how do you want me to proceed?”

00:04:07.799 --> 00:04:08.959
Hardy barked.

00:04:08.959 --> 00:04:12.599
“Uh, follow at a distance Agent Hardy,”
the operator replied.

00:04:12.599 --> 00:04:16.190
“Be advised do not engage with the creature
under any circumstances.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:21.470
It could be carrying any number of unknown
pathogens or diseases we don’t have cures

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:23.910
for, if it is from another universe.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:25.500
Strictly observation only.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:29.700
Mobile Task Force Null-6 is inbound to contain
your… alien.”

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:33.030
Agent Hardy turned and dashed out of the store,
sprinting down the street.

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:36.639
A little way in the distance, Venom had been
swinging from buildings.

00:04:36.639 --> 00:04:41.889
They were singing I Got You Under My Skin
to themselves without a care in the world,

00:04:41.889 --> 00:04:46.789
before landing on a rooftop and starting to
ravenously munch on their remaining chocolate

00:04:46.789 --> 00:04:47.789
bars.

00:04:47.789 --> 00:04:51.480
“Ahhh, delicious,” Venom growled after
finishing their feast.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:54.660
“So, when are we gonna work on getting back
home?”

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:58.990
Eddie asked, half of the symbiote’s protective
‘mask’ retracting to show him underneath.

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:00.850
“This might be our home!”

00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:01.850
Venom retorted.

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:04.990
“This planet looks the same in every universe.”

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:08.630
“Look, I really think we ought to prioritize
getting out of here!”

00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:10.280
the human half of them argued.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:13.150
“That should be our priority, not feeding
you!”

00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:20.110
“Eddie, we’ve been over this, I need phenethylamine
to live, and since you get all indignant at

00:05:20.110 --> 00:05:25.970
me for eating brains, we have to get it from
a more socially acceptable source,” the

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:27.590
alien creature replied.

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:28.600
“Unless…”

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:30.610
“Unless what?”

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:31.610
Brock asked.

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:34.840
“Unless you wanna go find some bad guys’
brains to eat?”

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:36.060
the symbiote queried.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:37.409
“Hey, you!”

00:05:37.409 --> 00:05:38.409
someone yelled.

00:05:38.409 --> 00:05:39.860
“Hold it right there!”

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:44.770
As if on cue, the sounds of weapons being
locked and loaded interrupted their conversation.

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:48.870
In the time since Agent Hardy had called it
in, The Foundation’s Mobile Task Force had

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:50.680
arrived on the rooftop.

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:55.430
Hardy was with them, hanging back and letting
the other operatives move in to apprehend

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:56.430
the alien.

00:05:56.430 --> 00:06:01.030
Drawing themselves to their full height, Venom
turned to face the approaching squad of armed

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:05.200
soldiers, their face returning to its full,
sharp-toothed form.

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:06.960
“Bad guys?”

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:08.789
Venom growled, grinning widely.

00:06:08.789 --> 00:06:13.350
“Guys with guns pointed at us, I’m gonna
guess probably bad guys,” Eddie answered,

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:16.160
before noticing the logo’s emblazoned on
the MTFs uniforms.

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:18.379
“Hold up, ‘SCP Foundation’?

00:06:18.379 --> 00:06:20.050
Like the Life Foundation?”

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:21.370
“Who cares?”

00:06:21.370 --> 00:06:22.699
Venom declared.

00:06:22.699 --> 00:06:24.030
“They’re dinner!”

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:25.350
“Open fire!”

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:29.680
the MTF commander yelled, before being suddenly
silenced – Venom had grabbed him and was

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:32.130
beginning to close his jaws around his head.

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:36.099
The remaining members of the task force followed
their squad leader’s final command and pulled

00:06:36.099 --> 00:06:37.199
their triggers.

00:06:37.199 --> 00:06:42.419
The rooftop erupted into a hail of gunfire,
bullets impacting with Venom’s oily form

00:06:42.419 --> 00:06:46.880
but causing no damage, bouncing off their
outer, gelatinous skin.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:51.250
They lunged at another of the MTF troopers,
wrenching the man’s weapon from his hands

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:54.800
and hurling it away, before grabbing him by
his ankle.

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:59.479
With incredible strength, Venom flung the
operative around in the air as if he was a

00:06:59.479 --> 00:07:04.009
ragdoll, swinging him into the other troops,
sending them flying.

00:07:04.009 --> 00:07:07.940
Hanging back from the fight, Agent Hardy was
trying to observe the creature’s attack

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:13.129
patterns; although it seemed to just be chaotically
flinging an MTF operative around as a weapon

00:07:13.129 --> 00:07:15.440
rather than deploying any form of actual technique.

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:20.259
He wanted to spot an opening, a weakness,
anything that could take down this hulking

00:07:20.259 --> 00:07:24.220
alien monster, but not one was presenting
itself.

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:28.730
That is, until Venom finished swinging that
helpless Foundation soldier around and threw

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:30.610
the man over their shoulder.

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:35.230
The MTF troop dropped limply down to street
level, landing on a parked car with a loud

00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:39.910
crash and the sound of glass shattering, which
was followed by the wailing of the car’s

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:41.350
emergency alarm.

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:45.860
The screeching noise seemingly caused Venom
to reel from their fight with the MTF, roaring

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:49.190
and gripping their head to drown out the alarm.

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:50.950
“Sound,” Hardy muttered to himself.

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:52.760
“Its weakness is sound.”

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:56.561
Instantly, he turned to one of the other MTF
soldiers and dashed towards him, while Venom

00:07:56.561 --> 00:07:59.139
was lashing out in an enraged state.

00:07:59.139 --> 00:08:04.220
The strands of the symbiote were recoiling,
exposing Eddie contained beneath.

00:08:04.220 --> 00:08:07.530
Agent Hardy grabbed the nearest Foundation
operative and violently struck him in the

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:11.780
face, taking advantage of the trooper’s
shock to pull his weapon out of his hands

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:14.319
and push him towards the edge of the rooftop.

00:08:14.319 --> 00:08:18.789
He delivered another blow, feeling his fellow
Foundation agent’s nose cracking against

00:08:18.789 --> 00:08:23.380
his fist as he took out all his frustrations
with his undercover posting.

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:27.669
The task force operative could barely believe
what was happening, too dumbfounded and in

00:08:27.669 --> 00:08:29.990
too much pain to protest.

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:35.250
Even when he did weakly lift his arms to defend
his face, Agent Hardy effortlessly swatted

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:40.380
them away and smashed his forehead into the
other agent’s face, dazing him as he dragged

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:42.080
him right up to the ledge.

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:47.080
There was nothing between the captive soldier,
just a sheer, multi-story drop down to street

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:48.080
level.

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:52.400
Lining him up, Agent Hardy shoved the other
man off the roof, so he landed on a second

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:53.400
car.

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:57.829
Its alarm started blaring, the horn too as
the fallen agent’s body went through the

00:08:57.829 --> 00:09:01.500
windshield, adding even more loud noises to
the mix.

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:06.440
Such a deafening combination of loud sounds
caused Venom to keel over, roaring in pain

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:08.660
as the symbiote’s main weakness pierced
it.

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:14.829
If the noise continued for too long, it would
force Eddie and his alien accomplice to separate,

00:09:14.829 --> 00:09:20.350
and so the slimy form defensively retreated
into its host, leaving him alone.

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:25.140
Wearing a triumphant, smug look on his face,
Agent Hardy marched over to the human being

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:26.140
that was left.

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:31.019
The alien form was gone, for now, meaning
he could just raise his stolen weapon and

00:09:31.019 --> 00:09:36.760
strike Eddie hard in the face, knocking him
out, ready for the Foundation to take him

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:39.760
– and the symbiote – in for examination.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:44.590
After hours of torture, that Agent Hardy had
volunteered to conduct personally, the Foundation

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:49.709
had learned that a sustained barrage of high-frequency
soundwaves could be used to forcibly separate

00:09:49.709 --> 00:09:52.820
the gelatinous alien life form from its host.

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:57.320
Once they had been parted, Eddie Brock didn’t
need much more containment than any other

00:09:57.320 --> 00:10:02.459
average human; while the symbiote could be
placed in a glass tank for Foundation researchers

00:10:02.459 --> 00:10:04.060
to take a closer look at.

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:09.360
“The creature seems to possess a consciousness,
its own mobility; it's an entirely separate

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:14.519
entity from Mr. Brock,” one of the researchers
commented, observing a sample of the symbiote

00:10:14.519 --> 00:10:19.350
that they had managed to slice off the larger
whole, and was now slithering its way around

00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:21.670
a smaller, transparent containment cube.

00:10:21.670 --> 00:10:25.350
“That’s pretty obvious, Poindexter,”
Agent Hardy retorted impatiently.

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:28.220
“Why don’t you give me something useful?”

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:33.110
“W-well,” the researcher stammered, intimidated
by the imposing field operative.

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:35.329
“It appears to be rapidly deteriorating.”

00:10:35.329 --> 00:10:37.160
“That thing is dying?”

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:38.160
Hardy asked.

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:39.160
“It seems so.

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:43.480
We’ve been able to access some sort of hive
mind that it shares with the rest of its kind.

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:46.040
Apparently, these…” he checked his notes.

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:49.850
“Klyntar are able to share knowledge across
multiple realities.

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:54.880
But they need to remain bonded to a host in
order to survive, on their own their lifespans

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:57.050
are much shorter,” the researcher added.

00:10:57.050 --> 00:11:01.600
“But it seems that, once they have, they
increase the host’s strength, replicate

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:05.600
their own mass, even use more of itself to
create weapons.”

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:06.750
“Weapons?”

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:08.190
the Agent echoed.

00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:09.440
“Yes, yes.

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:13.130
Anything, it seems some of these symbiotes
could even create copies of existing weaponry,

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:17.730
that would act as extensions of itself, fully
useable by the host.”

00:11:17.730 --> 00:11:18.760
“Thank you, Doc.

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:21.079
That info should come in pretty handy…”

00:11:21.079 --> 00:11:22.090
Agent Hardy replied.

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:24.990
“I b-beg your pardon, Agent?”

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:29.139
the researcher asked, before Agent Hardy’s
hand gripping his throat silenced him.

00:11:29.139 --> 00:11:33.840
Elsewhere in the facility, Eddie Brock was
yelling, demanding to be let free.

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:37.839
His only thought was getting back to Venom,
aware that his symbiote partner would wither

00:11:37.839 --> 00:11:40.310
and die if they remained apart for too long.

00:11:40.310 --> 00:11:46.011
Thanks to their bond, he knew Venom was thinking
the same at this precise moment, and it only

00:11:46.011 --> 00:11:48.730
spurred him on to try and pull himself free.

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:51.600
He was handcuffed to a chair, barely able
to move.

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:56.160
Normally, the pair of them could get out of
a jam like this with no trouble; after all,

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:58.730
things were always easier when they were together.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:00.010
“I got you!”

00:12:00.010 --> 00:12:02.320
Eddie started to sing, loudly and tunelessly.

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:03.889
“Under my skin!”

00:12:03.889 --> 00:12:04.889
“Quiet!”

00:12:04.889 --> 00:12:08.390
snapped a Foundation security officer who
stood nearby.

00:12:08.390 --> 00:12:12.710
“I got you,” he ignored the guard and
continued, making his voice even louder.

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:15.399
“Deep in the heart of me!

00:12:15.399 --> 00:12:20.280
So deep in my heart that you’re really a
part of me!

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:22.000
I got you…”

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:23.900
“I said, quiet!”

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:28.040
the officer barked, marching over to Eddie,
baton raised threateningly.

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:32.040
With a sudden, unrelenting strike, he kicked
the guard in the stomach with all the force

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:33.040
he could manage.

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:37.209
Winded, the officer crumpled, dropping to
the floor as he gasped for air.

00:12:37.209 --> 00:12:42.079
Not letting up, Eddie kicked again, this time
his boot connected with the man’s jaw and

00:12:42.079 --> 00:12:43.079
knocked him out.

00:12:43.079 --> 00:12:47.649
It wouldn’t last forever though; using his
legs, and with a great deal of difficulty

00:12:47.649 --> 00:12:51.190
Eddie tried to lift the handcuff keys from
the officer’s belt.

00:12:51.190 --> 00:12:56.250
He hardly possessed perfect coordination,
meaning it required a lot of trial and error,

00:12:56.250 --> 00:13:01.130
but knowing Venom needed him made him all
the more determined to try again and again.

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:07.170
Until, finally, Eddie pulled the keys up with
his boots, lifted his legs, so they slid down,

00:13:07.170 --> 00:13:09.570
and caught them in his cuffed hand.

00:13:09.570 --> 00:13:13.910
Freeing himself, he left the unconscious security
guard cuffed in his place, before making his

00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:17.680
way through the facility as quickly and quietly
as he could.

00:13:17.680 --> 00:13:22.899
It didn’t matter that he had never been
there before, he could sense Venom anywhere;

00:13:22.899 --> 00:13:27.370
even though they were apart, all he had to
do was follow the pull to where it was being

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:28.370
held.

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:32.200
However, he could’ve done with his symbiote
partner’s protection when he arrived in

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:33.430
the lab.

00:13:33.430 --> 00:13:37.500
Something tore through Eddie’s shoulder,
embedding itself in his flesh.

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:41.580
Screaming with pain, he lifted a hand to the
bleeding wound, only to feel a second shot

00:13:41.580 --> 00:13:42.940
strike him in the gut.

00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:47.769
He could feel the projectile in his hand;
gritting his teeth, he pulled it out.

00:13:47.769 --> 00:13:51.400
It was a tooth, blood-soaked, and fired with
the force of a bullet.

00:13:51.400 --> 00:13:55.160
It was then that Eddie looked up and saw where
from.

00:13:55.160 --> 00:13:58.250
Towering over him, Agent Hardy looked almost
unrecognizable.

00:13:58.250 --> 00:14:03.820
He had bonded with the sample cut off the
symbiote, and it had encased his body in a

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:05.070
suit all of his own.

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:10.670
His had black, segmented plates, like armor,
although with the same gelatinous, oily appearance

00:14:10.670 --> 00:14:11.670
as Venom.

00:14:11.670 --> 00:14:17.240
In his hands was what looked like a submachine
gun, but was, in actuality, something special

00:14:17.240 --> 00:14:21.420
the agent had requisitioned from the Foundation’s
anomalous armory.

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:28.570
It was SCP-127, a weapon that – like the
symbiote – was also an organic, living being,

00:14:28.570 --> 00:14:32.230
capable of firing human-like teeth in the
place of bullets.

00:14:32.230 --> 00:14:36.959
To make matters worse, the shred of symbiote
Hardy wore had cloned its own versions of

00:14:36.959 --> 00:14:43.200
SCP-127, their handles extending into long,
black tendrils that protruded from the agent’s

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:44.200
back.

00:14:44.200 --> 00:14:48.220
The rest of Venom was still contained in a
tank, frantically slithering against the glass,

00:14:48.220 --> 00:14:49.769
trying to free itself and get to Eddie.

00:14:49.769 --> 00:14:54.040
If it did, it could heal his injuries and
make itself whole again.

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:58.639
Stomping over to where his wounded victim
lay, Symbiote-infused Hardy pulled Eddie up

00:14:58.639 --> 00:15:03.000
from the floor and lifted him off his feet,
making sure he dug his symbiote-coated thumb

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:07.000
into his wounds, making Eddie cry out in pain.

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:10.750
“Gotta be said, Mr. Brock,” Hardy grinned
sadistically.

00:15:10.750 --> 00:15:15.070
“I can see why you’d want to be merged
with one of these things.

00:15:15.070 --> 00:15:19.339
The strength it gives you is… amazing!

00:15:19.339 --> 00:15:25.580
Enough to make anybody take you seriously,
remind them not to underestimate you.

00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:31.130
And that’s all from me getting a little
piece, imagine how strong I’ll be when I’m

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:33.630
combined with your little alien friend there.”

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:36.199
“You should know,” Eddie winced.

00:15:36.199 --> 00:15:39.300
“Venom’s a little picky about who he hangs
out with.

00:15:39.300 --> 00:15:42.320
And trust me, you’re not his type.”

00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:43.339
“Oh yeah?”

00:15:43.339 --> 00:15:44.500
Agent Hardy roared.

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:49.020
With his symbiote-enhanced strength, he hurled
Eddie across the lab with such force that

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:53.540
he smashed the glass tank, before colliding
with the far wall and landing in a heap.

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:57.839
Eddie was still bleeding heavily from the
teeth he’d been shot with, as Venom tried

00:15:57.839 --> 00:16:02.040
– in its weakened state – to slide across
the floor towards him… only for Hardy to

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:03.040
catch it.

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:06.959
He lifted the rest of the dark, gooey symbiote
up and dangled it tauntingly over Eddie as

00:16:06.959 --> 00:16:09.120
he lay bleeding out on the floor.

00:16:09.120 --> 00:16:13.540
“You’re nothing without this thing attached
to you, Brock,” Hardy jeered.

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:20.990
“In fact, even when you were bonded on that
rooftop, you were easy enough to take down.

00:16:20.990 --> 00:16:26.300
Guess even together, you two are nothing.”

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:31.600
“N-no,” Eddie rasped weakly, reaching
his hand up with the last of his fading strength;

00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:35.730
as he did, Hardy didn’t notice the symbiote
reaching back to its host.

00:16:35.730 --> 00:16:37.540
“Together we’re… we’re a…”

00:16:37.540 --> 00:16:40.970
The alien life form gave a surge, and slipped
over Eddie’s hand.

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:45.880
Instantly, his gunshot wounds sealed up and
repaired, just as the dark, slimy form encased

00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:46.970
him once more.

00:16:46.970 --> 00:16:50.880
Standing up, catching Hardy by surprise, Venom
gripped the Agent by the neck.

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:54.750
“We’re a Lethal Protector, you feel me?”

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:58.529
they growled, grinning and showing off their
sharp rows of teeth.

00:16:58.529 --> 00:17:01.899
Venom lifted Agent Hardy up and threw him
hard enough to send him crashing through the

00:17:01.899 --> 00:17:03.680
wall, landing a few feet away.

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:06.080
“Glad to have you back,” came Eddie’s
voice.

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:08.010
“Good to be back!”

00:17:08.010 --> 00:17:09.010
Venom replied.

00:17:09.010 --> 00:17:11.400
“Were you singing our song earlier?”

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:12.699
“Yeah,” Eddie sighed.

00:17:12.699 --> 00:17:14.530
“That’s how I escaped.”

00:17:14.530 --> 00:17:18.440
Before they could continue their conversation,
Agent Hardy roared at them.

00:17:18.440 --> 00:17:24.080
Staggering back to his feet, he began firing
SCP-127 at Venom, the various copies his symbiote

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:27.700
had created unleashing a barrage of toothy
projectiles at them.

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:31.820
They didn’t ricochet off like regular bullets,
in fact they seemed to be strong enough to

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:36.280
shred through Venom’s outer symbiote skin,
until it had a chance to reform.

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:37.280
“Ouch!”

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:38.280
they roared.

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:40.460
“Oh yeah, his guns shoot teeth!”

00:17:40.460 --> 00:17:42.510
Eddie warned, slightly too late.

00:17:42.510 --> 00:17:44.280
“This guy sucks!”

00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:45.280
Venom growled.

00:17:45.280 --> 00:17:46.929
“No arguments there,” Eddie replied.

00:17:46.929 --> 00:17:48.730
“You got a plan here, partner?”

00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:51.299
“I am open to suggestions, Eddie!”

00:17:51.299 --> 00:17:56.289
the symbiotic half answered as they retreated
from the gunfire, Hardy charging after them.

00:17:56.289 --> 00:18:00.309
The Agent lunged at them, tackling Venom,
pinning them down and delivering a vicious

00:18:00.309 --> 00:18:01.309
punch.

00:18:01.309 --> 00:18:04.570
The force of it split the symbiote head apart,
revealing Eddie beneath.

00:18:04.570 --> 00:18:07.760
“You don’t deserve this much power!”

00:18:07.760 --> 00:18:12.700
Agent Hardy yelled, lifting one of his oily
black tooth-firing guns to Eddie’s exposed

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:13.700
face.

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:18.580
Just as he fired, Venom’s ‘mask’ reformed,
in the nick of time to protect its host.

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:22.840
As the tooth impacted their face, both Eddie
and his symbiote partner noticed something.

00:18:22.840 --> 00:18:28.250
Hardy’s symbiote seemed to suffer the same
damage, slickly parting and then quickly reforming.

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:30.860
“He’s just wearing a part of you, right,
V?”

00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:31.860
Eddie asked.

00:18:31.860 --> 00:18:33.409
“When we get hurt, he gets hurt!

00:18:33.409 --> 00:18:36.409
We just need to hurt him enough to get them
to separate, and you can get that part of

00:18:36.409 --> 00:18:37.760
your body back!”

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:41.170
Venom lifted their head, noticing a button
on the wall of the corridor.

00:18:41.170 --> 00:18:45.980
The Foundation had plenty of need for emergency
alarms in case an anomaly broke containment,

00:18:45.980 --> 00:18:51.090
and sure enough, there was one labeled ‘Activate
in Case of Emergency’.

00:18:51.090 --> 00:18:55.280
Raising one arm, Venom fired a line of organic
web at the button.

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:59.470
The screaming, ringing sound had both Venom
and Agent Hardy writing in agony.

00:18:59.470 --> 00:19:04.050
The symbiote began retracting from the Foundation
field agent as the alarm blared.

00:19:04.050 --> 00:19:08.429
He weakly tried to crawl towards it, desperate
to switch it off before his suit separated

00:19:08.429 --> 00:19:09.429
from him.

00:19:09.429 --> 00:19:13.570
A fist sailed through the air and clocked
Hardy square in the jaw: Eddie had landed

00:19:13.570 --> 00:19:14.570
a hit.

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:18.450
He’d knocked Hardy over, keeping him down
for long enough so that the portion of the

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:22.640
symbiote that had been removed leaped off
the agent’s body, and quickly crawled its

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:25.050
way back to its original host.

00:19:25.050 --> 00:19:30.190
Shutting the alarm off again, Eddie was once
again encased in the form of the Lethal Protector,

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:36.130
and they towered over Agent Hardy, long, slimy
tongue unraveling from their razor-toothed

00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:37.130
jaws.

00:19:37.130 --> 00:19:39.830
“Just who in the hell do you think you are?”

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:41.880
Hardy spat, enraged.

00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:42.880
“We…

00:19:42.880 --> 00:19:44.520
are Venom.”

00:19:44.520 --> 00:19:48.460
Agent Hardy’s screams echoed through the
halls of the site, then quickly fell silent

00:19:48.460 --> 00:19:50.060
with a meaty crunch.

00:19:50.060 --> 00:19:54.450
Not long after, Venom noticed that they were
starting to fade from this universe again.

00:19:54.450 --> 00:19:58.049
“Uh, Eddie, it’s happening again,” Venom
exclaimed.

00:19:58.049 --> 00:20:00.700
“We’d better end up home this time!”

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:05.120
Eddie sighed as they disappeared, leaving
the Foundation to clean up the mess they’d

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:06.220
left behind.

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:10.520
Now go check out “ SCP Elite Mobile Task
Force Explained” and “How to Work at the

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:15.669
SCP Foundation Explained” if, much like
Agent Hardy, you need a crash course in how

00:20:15.669 --> 00:20:19.200
a proper SCP Foundation operative should behave!

